  "statement": "Let $a=2+\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=2-\\sqrt{3}$. (i) Show that $a+b=4$ and $ab=1$. (ii) Define $s_{n}=a^{n}+b^{n}$ for $n\\ge 0$. Show that $s_{n}=4s_{n-1}-s_{n-2}$ for all $n\\ge 2$. (iii) Hence find $s_{6}$.",
  "solution": "(i) $a+b=4$, $ab=(2+\\sqrt{3})(2-\\sqrt{3})=4-3=1$. (ii) $a,b$ are roots of $t^{2}-4t+1=0$, so $a^{2}=4a-1$ and $b^{2}=4b-1$. Multiplying by $a^{n-2}$ gives $a^{n}=4a^{n-1}-a^{n-2}$; similarly for $b$. Adding yields $s_{n}=4s_{n-1}-s_{n-2}$. (iii) $s_{0}=2$, $s_{1}=4$, then $s_{2}=14$, $s_{3}=52$, $s_{4}=194$, $s_{5}=724$, $s_{6}=4\\cdot724-194=2702$.",
  "solutionStatus": "full",
  "hints": [
    "Form the quadratic with roots a,b.",
    "Multiply the relation by a^{n-2}."
  ],
  "_difficultyNote": "[难度自评: Q1是 Q2是 Q3是 Q4是 Q5否 → 5星]"
